Subject: register VM: add-transition put inline cache

What this does:
  Extends the register VM's store inline cache with a second entry kind
  (REG_PIC_ADD_W) that caches an own-property *add*: the pre-add shape and the
  fresh property's slot. The store PIC has two ways per site and the add kind
  uses the secondary way, so an existing overwrite cache (REG_PIC_OWN_W) is
  never disturbed.

  regvm_put_field_ic snapshots the pre-add shape before the engine write and
  hands it to regvm_put_pic_fill, which records `pre-add shape -> post-add shape`
  when the write created exactly one fresh plain writable own data slot.
  regvm_put_field_add_hit replays that transition without calling the engine:
  it re-checks the shape, extensibility, non-exoticness and the prototype
  watchpoint epoch (stashed in the entry's spare field), grows the property
  array if needed, installs the cached shape and writes the slot. A store site
  only snapshots when its secondary way is empty or already matches the receiver
  shape, so a polymorphic site does not thrash the cache.

  Mirrored in the monolith handler and in the generated step helpers
  (quickjs-regvm-step.inc, regenerated). The regeneration also picks up a stale
  sub_imm_s / sub_imm_self_s float-overflow branch that had been fixed in the
  monolith but not re-emitted (`+ imm` -> `- imm`).

Why we need it:
  `obj.x = v` on a fresh object is common in constructors and object literals;
  every such store previously fell back to JS_SetPropertyInternal2, whose
  add-property path walks the shape/prototype chain and installs a transition.
  Caching the add removes that engine round-trip. Measured on the deterministic
  corpus (instructions:u, same-binary on/off): raytrace -23.5%, earleyboyer
  -19.2%, typescript -6.1%, deltablue -2.6%, box2d -2.4%, splay -2.3%; no row
  regresses. The add path is hit 31.8M times in earleyboyer and 17.0M in
  raytrace.

Needs a bytecode version bump: No

Notes:
  - The register PIC entry is 16 bytes and the epoch fits in the spare uint16
    misses field (JS_IC_EPOCH_MAX = 0x1fff).
  - The transition is sound only while no interceptor has appeared on a
    prototype since the fill, which the epoch guard enforces.
  - The step helpers are generated by .local/regvm-build/emit-step.py; the .inc
    diff includes the two sub_imm float fixes described above.

